# This checkout has core.autocrlf enabled, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout for anything Git considers text. That is fine for source, and not
# fine for files whose bytes are the payload.
#
# The Apple Pay association file is a hex-encoded JSON blob with no line
# terminators. Nothing to convert today, but a stray newline introduced later
# would be checked out as CRLF and Apple would reject the domain.
.well-known/** -text

# A vCard is CRLF by specification (RFC 6350). Left to normalise, the repo
# would hold LF and a Linux build agent would check out and ship LF, which the
# stricter phone contact importers reject.
*.vcf -text

# Fonts and images are binary; never line-ending convert or diff them.
*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
